{%- comment -%}
  Senseless OS class — stamps ss-os-ios / ss-os-android on <html> once, in the
  head (2026-07-28). Companion to senseless-wallet-gate (same placement).

  Why a root class and not per-component JS: the cart drawer is AJAX-injected on
  every cart re-render, and inline <script> inserted as HTML never executes
  (same constraint documented in senseless-cart-offer). The device OS never
  changes mid-session, so one parse-time classification lets every app-badge
  surface (cart banner, /pages/app) be pure CSS — no re-run needed.

  Classification: iPhone/iPad/iPod UA ⇒ ios; "Macintosh" + multi-touch ⇒ ios
  (iPadOS 13+ masquerades as macOS Safari); Android UA ⇒ android. Desktop and
  anything unrecognised gets neither class — surfaces then show BOTH store
  badges, which is the correct no-JS fallback too.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    try {
      var ua = navigator.userAgent || '';
      var cls = '';
      if (/iPhone|iPad|iPod/.test(ua)) {
        cls = 'ss-os-ios';
      } else if (/Macintosh/.test(ua) && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 1) {
        cls = 'ss-os-ios';
      } else if (/Android/.test(ua)) {
        cls = 'ss-os-android';
      }
      if (cls) document.documentElement.classList.add(cls);
    } catch (e) { /* leave unclassified — both badges render */ }
  })();
</script>
